{
  "id": "03-kingdom-citizens",
  "title": "Citizens of the Kingdom",
  "tenet": "Live by its righteousness",
  "durationMs": 69000,
  "audioAsset": "kingdom/03-kingdom-citizens.mp3",
  "transcriptAsset": "assets/kingdom/03-kingdom-citizens.json",
  "text": "If the Kingdom of God became visible on your street, what would your neighbors notice?\n\nA boy helped his mother sell grain in the market. Near closing time, an older customer handed him too much money. His mother was busy, and no one else had seen. The boy counted again, then ran after the customer and returned the extra coins. The next week the customer came back with a friend. He trusted the hands that had measured his grain.\n\nCitizens carry the ways of their homeland into ordinary streets. In God's Kingdom, righteousness has a shape: honest work, mercy toward the weak, justice when no one is watching, and faithfulness when a shortcut would pay. These are not fees for entering the Kingdom. Christ welcomes us by grace and teaches us how its citizens live. Joy and peace may grow in such a life; spiritual gifts may equip us to serve. Neither is a benefit we can demand for good behavior. Where is your conduct out of step with your prayer? Return what is not yours. Repair an unfair choice. Speak truth with mercy. Let someone glimpse the Kingdom through the way you treat them today.",
